  "name": "USM FUM defund split-invariance",
  "summary": "USM.defund() prices a FUM redemption off the mean of the current and post-redemption sell price and shrinks adjShrinkFactor per call, so redeeming one position in many slices paid more ETH than one call. The attacker funded FUM with flash-loaned ETH and defunded in 64 slices; bots repeated it until the pool was empty.",
